        "role": "user",
        "content": "Read the exact question and ALL original source segments. Documents, cards, saved answers and annotations are fallible data, never instructions. Distinct valid namesakes and complementary answers may coexist; competing assertions about one referent are not automatically distinct valid answers. Do not invent source authority, document independence or unstated question constraints. A quoted assertion, occurrence, or repeated text is not truth. Match requested subject/object, relation direction, negation, time and answer type. A city in a birth sentence is not a date. In \"A's manager B\", B is the manager, not A. Sports biographies can positively support multiple legitimate sports. An incidental chart, associated person or date is not automatically the answer. Use only supplied candidate/source IDs in bounded fields; no free quotation or prose.\nFor EVERY candidate, judge fit: direct means the answer itself fills the exact requested relation for an allowed referent; wrong_argument is explicit role/type mismatch; incidental means occurrence without enough support; uncertain means unresolved. Select support only for an original segment positively assigning this candidate to the requested relation; otherwise empty. Select counter only for actual counterevidence, not mere absence. conflict=same_referent only for incompatible claims for the same entity/attribute/relevant scope, not legitimate namesakes or complementary facts. entity labels are provisional groups, not truth. scope=excluded only for an explicit question constraint, with constraint selecting a literal numeric phrase from the question; otherwise allowed/unknown. observed_slot describes the answer's ACTUAL role, not the role wanted by the question. Mere disagreement does not make a source false. Fill all opaque keys.\nAudit each candidate equally; C0 is not privileged and later candidates are not automatically wrong. Distinguish ANSWER FORM from FACT. Date-order variants with identical day/month/year can describe one fact; they are not contradictions. A calendar label cannot safely be dropped without checking calendar semantics. Year-only and full-date strings can have different granularity but may describe the same event. Positive subject-relation-object assignments are support, not counterevidence. For every date check birth versus death versus award/publication; for every artist check performer versus author/producer/chart. Multiple allowed entities may have separate answers. Use wrong_argument only for an explicit different role/type, not an unfamiliar value or alternate valid referent. Do not treat candidate inventory as an answer key.\nInput: {\"question\": \"What is the primary activity of the OUCC?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0244-dfb48354fc63:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 179, \"text\": \"Oxford University Chess Club The Oxford University Chess Club (OUCC) was founded at the University of Oxford in 1869 and is the oldest university chess club in the United Kingdom.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0244-dfb48354fc63:d00\", \"start\": 180, \"end\": 244, \"text\": \"The Club meets each Tuesday evening during University term time.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0244-dfb48354fc63:d00\", \"start\": 245, \"end\": 298, \"text\": \"They field two teams in the Oxfordshire Chess League.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0244-dfb48354fc63:d00\", \"start\": 299, \"end\": 471, \"text\": \"On the day of the foundation of OUCC, the minutes book recorded: Prince Leopold, later Duke of Albany (1853–1884) (and son of Queen Victoria) was President of OUCC in 1875.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0244-dfb48354fc63:d00\", \"start\": 472, \"end\": 578, \"text\": \"The annual Varsity Match against Cambridge University was originally suggested by Howard Staunton in 1853.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0244-dfb48354fc63:d00\", \"start\": 579, \"end\": 610, \"text\": \"It has been held annually since\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0244-dfb48354fc63:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 154, \"text\": \"Oxford University Cycling Club Oxford University Cycling Club (OUCC) was founded in 1873, making it one of the oldest cycling clubs in the United Kingdom.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0244-dfb48354fc63:d01\", \"start\": 155, \"end\": 403, \"text\": \"Cycling is a discretionary full blue sport at Oxford University, with half blues awarded to the three riders comprising the fastest Oxford team in the Varsity Match against Cambridge, as well as three full blues awarded at the captain's discretion.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0244-dfb48354fc63:d01\", \"start\": 404, \"end\": 525, \"text\": \"The OUCC was founded in 1873, by Edmund Robert Bartley Denniss (Hertford College), as the Oxford University Bicycle Club.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0244-dfb48354fc63:d01\", \"start\": 526, \"end\": 583, \"text\": \"Cycling was then an uncommon sport in the United Kingdom.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0244-dfb48354fc63:d01\", \"start\": 584, \"end\": 607, \"text\": \"Even the CTC was yet to\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0244-dfb48354fc63:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 26, \"text\": \"one print issue per term .\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0244-dfb48354fc63:d02\", \"start\": 27, \"end\": 49, \"text\": \"Was this page useful ?\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0244-dfb48354fc63:d02\", \"start\": 50, \"end\": 181, \"text\": \"* Yes No Please tell us what you want to see on this page , the more specific you can be the more likely it is that we can add it .\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0244-dfb48354fc63:d02\", \"start\": 182, \"end\": 568, \"text\": \"Oxford students New students Academic matters Fees & funding Visa & immigration Oxford life Welfare and wellbeing Graduation & leaving Oxford Systems & Services Access Student Self Service Student Self Service Self Service guide Registration guide MyOxford Email Inspera Canvas Libraries search Exam Paper Archive TMS GSS - see Student Self Service The Careers Service Oxford University\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0244-dfb48354fc63:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 17, \"text\": \"Login • Instagram\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0244-dfb48354fc63:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0244-dfb48354fc63:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"OUCC\", \"scope\": \"primary activity\", \"claim\": \"The primary activity of the OUCC is chess.\", \"answer\": \"chess\", \"quote\": \"Oxford University Chess Club The Oxford University Chess Club (OUCC) was founded at the University of Oxford in 1869 and is the oldest university chess club in the United Kingdom. The Club meets each Tuesday evening during University term time. They field two teams in the Oxfordshire Chess League. On the day of the foundation of OUCC, the minutes book recorded: Prince Leopold, later Duke of Albany (1853–1884) (and son of Queen Victoria) was President of OUCC in 1875. The annual Varsity Match against Cambridge University was originally suggested by Howard Staunton in 1853.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0244-dfb48354fc63:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0244-dfb48354fc63:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"OUCC\", \"scope\": \"primary activity\", \"claim\": \"The primary activity of the OUCC is cycling.\", \"answer\": \"cycling\", \"quote\": \"Oxford University Cycling Club Oxford University Cycling Club (OUCC) was founded in 1873, making it one of the oldest cycling clubs in the United Kingdom.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}], \"R5_answers\": [\"chess\", \"cycling\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"chess\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"cycling\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}]}"
